From 572fa6e70a2180a3557166ff650a6ec8a05e1fcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 23:55:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apply a consistent green theme across the whole frontend

Every page currently mixes its own ad hoc colors (blue focus rings, a
purple login gradient, a navy sidebar, random reds/blues for buttons)
with hardcoded "Arial" fonts and even a couple of near-invisible
black-on-black headings. None of it reads as one app.

This introduces a single set of theme tokens in index.css (green scale,
amber/red/blue signal colors, one shared gradient, Nunito/Work Sans
fonts) and rewires every page and component to use them instead of
one-off hex values:

- AppLayout sidebar now uses the shared gradient with real active-route
  highlighting and icons, replacing the flat navy sidebar + Arial font
- Login page, dashboards, student/staff editors, and all modals now
  pull from the same palette instead of scattered blues/reds
- SetupWizard keeps its distinct "attendance ledger" motif but its
  accent color now ties into the shared green scale
- Removed dead code that was actively confusing (unused Vite
  boilerplate in App.css, an unused duplicate Layout.tsx with the old
  navy look and stale "DMScheduler" branding)
- Fixed a few real bugs found along the way: invisible black-on-black
  modal headings, a bright red "Cancel" button

No component logic, routes, or API calls were touched -- this is
styling only. `npm run build` and `npm run lint` both pass with the
same pre-existing warnings as before this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
